# Architecture Decision Records

</div>

<div align = "justify">

The architecture decision records capture why each important decision was made and what follows from it. Each file is
named `XXXX-imperative-title.md`, where `XXXX` is a sequence number that follows the Nygard format. The layout builds
on [MADR (Markdown Any Decision Records)](https://adr.github.io/madr/), tailored for large repositories.

<div align = "center">

| ADR # | Decision Slug | ADR Status | Document Tag(s) |
| :---: | --- | :---: | :---: |

</div>

The ADR Status flag always shows a record's current state: (I) 🚧: ADR document is proposed, (II) ✅: ADR document is
accepted, (III) ❌: ADR document is deprecated, and (IV) 🛠️: ADR document is superseded with a new decision. The table
below pairs each replaced record with its replacement, and it stays empty until a decision is replaced.

<div align = "center">

| Previous ADR File | Updated ADR File |
| :---: | :---: |

</div>

A coding assistant finds the relevant records by their tags, then reads how and why each decision was made and what it
asks for, together with the dated additional changes near the top of a record, which extend its decision. When a newer
record replaces an older one, the assistant reads the newer record in full before it acts on the decision, and never
reverts to the older one on its own.

</div>
